Feature: Reserve stock
  The order system reserves every line in full, or nothing. The shell loads the stored level of each
  SKU-location pair of the lines, and the open reservation of the order, if there is one.

  Scenario: Every line is reserved in full
    When I run "reserve_stock" with:
      | caller.role  | now                      | idempotency_key | order_id | reserve_lines                                                                                                                 | stored_levels                                                                                                                                                                                     |
      | order_system | 2026-11-22T10:00:00.000Z | reserve-0001    | ORD-1    | [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "quantity": 10}, {"sku": "GADGET-2", "location": "AMS-B-0143", "quantity": 5}] | [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "on_hand": 500, "reserved": 100, "available": 400}, {"sku": "GADGET-2", "location": "AMS-B-0143", "on_hand": 50, "reserved": 40, "available": 10}] |
    Then the output is "reservation_made":
      | result   | levels                                                                                                                                                                                           | depletions |
      | RESERVED | [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "on_hand": 500, "reserved": 110, "available": 390}, {"sku": "GADGET-2", "location": "AMS-B-0143", "on_hand": 50, "reserved": 45, "available": 5}] | []         |

  Scenario: A line that takes the last available units depletes its stock
    When I run "reserve_stock" with:
      | caller.role  | now                      | idempotency_key | order_id | reserve_lines                                                   | stored_levels                                                                                   |
      | order_system | 2026-11-22T10:00:00.000Z | reserve-0001    | ORD-1    | [{"sku": "GADGET-2", "location": "AMS-B-0143", "quantity": 10}] | [{"sku": "GADGET-2", "location": "AMS-B-0143", "on_hand": 50, "reserved": 40, "available": 10}] |
    Then the output is "reservation_made":
      | result   | levels                                                                                         |
      | RESERVED | [{"sku": "GADGET-2", "location": "AMS-B-0143", "on_hand": 50, "reserved": 50, "available": 0}] |

  Scenario Outline: A time-to-live sets the expiry
    When I run "reserve_stock" with:
      | caller.role  | now                      | idempotency_key | order_id | reserve_lines                                                                                                                 | stored_levels                                                                                                                                                                                     | ttl_minutes   |
      | order_system | 2026-11-22T10:00:00.000Z | reserve-0001    | ORD-1    | [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "quantity": 10}, {"sku": "GADGET-2", "location": "AMS-B-0143", "quantity": 5}] | [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "on_hand": 500, "reserved": 100, "available": 400}, {"sku": "GADGET-2", "location": "AMS-B-0143", "on_hand": 50, "reserved": 40, "available": 10}] | <ttl_minutes> |
    Then the output is "reservation_made":
      | result   |
      | RESERVED |

    Examples:
      | ttl_minutes |
      | 1           |
      | 10080       |

  Scenario: A line that the stock cannot cover reserves nothing
    When I run "reserve_stock" with:
      | caller.role  | now                      | idempotency_key | order_id | reserve_lines                                                                                                                  | stored_levels                                                                                                                                                                                     |
      | order_system | 2026-11-22T10:00:00.000Z | reserve-0001    | ORD-1    | [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "quantity": 10}, {"sku": "GADGET-2", "location": "AMS-B-0143", "quantity": 11}] | [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "on_hand": 500, "reserved": 100, "available": 400}, {"sku": "GADGET-2", "location": "AMS-B-0143", "on_hand": 50, "reserved": 40, "available": 10}] |
    Then the output is "insufficient_stock":
      | error_code         | short_lines                                                                       |
      | INSUFFICIENT_STOCK | [{"sku": "GADGET-2", "location": "AMS-B-0143", "requested": 11, "available": 10}] |

  Scenario Outline: An order with an open reservation gets no second one
    When I run "reserve_stock" with:
      | caller.role  | now                      | idempotency_key | order_id | reserve_lines                                                                                                                 | stored_levels                                                                                                                                                                                     | open_reservation   |
      | order_system | 2026-11-22T10:00:00.000Z | reserve-0001    | ORD-1    | [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "quantity": 10}, {"sku": "GADGET-2", "location": "AMS-B-0143", "quantity": 5}] | [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "on_hand": 500, "reserved": 100, "available": 400}, {"sku": "GADGET-2", "location": "AMS-B-0143", "on_hand": 50, "reserved": 40, "available": 10}] | <open_reservation> |
    Then the output is "open_reservation_exists":
      | error_code      | order_id |
      | INVALID_REQUEST | ORD-1    |

    Examples:
      | open_reservation                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |
      | {"reservation_id": "9c1d2e3f-4a5b-4c6d-8e7f-0a1b2c3d4e5f", "order_id": "ORD-1", "state": "ACTIVE", "reservation_lines": [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "quantity": 10, "shipped": 0}, {"sku": "GADGET-2", "location": "AMS-B-0143", "quantity": 5, "shipped": 0}], "expires_at": "2026-11-22T10:30:00.000Z"}            |
      | {"reservation_id": "9c1d2e3f-4a5b-4c6d-8e7f-0a1b2c3d4e5f", "order_id": "ORD-1", "state": "PARTIALLY_SHIPPED", "reservation_lines": [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "quantity": 10, "shipped": 4}, {"sku": "GADGET-2", "location": "AMS-B-0143", "quantity": 5, "shipped": 5}], "expires_at": "2026-11-22T10:30:00.000Z"} |

  Scenario: A line of an unknown SKU is refused
    When I run "reserve_stock" with:
      | caller.role  | now                      | idempotency_key | order_id | reserve_lines                                                     | stored_levels                                                                                                                                                                                     |
      | order_system | 2026-11-22T10:00:00.000Z | reserve-0001    | ORD-1    | [{"sku": "NO-SUCH-SKU", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "quantity": 5}] | [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "on_hand": 500, "reserved": 100, "available": 400}, {"sku": "GADGET-2", "location": "AMS-B-0143", "on_hand": 50, "reserved": 40, "available": 10}] |
    Then the output is "unknown_sku":
      | error_code  | sku         |
      | UNKNOWN_SKU | NO-SUCH-SKU |

  Scenario: A line at an unknown location is refused
    When I run "reserve_stock" with:
      | caller.role  | now                      | idempotency_key | order_id | reserve_lines                                                  | stored_levels                                                                                                                                                                                     |
      | order_system | 2026-11-22T10:00:00.000Z | reserve-0001    | ORD-1    | [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "ZZZ-Z-9999", "quantity": 5}] | [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "on_hand": 500, "reserved": 100, "available": 400}, {"sku": "GADGET-2", "location": "AMS-B-0143", "on_hand": 50, "reserved": 40, "available": 10}] |
    Then the output is "unknown_location":
      | error_code       | location   |
      | UNKNOWN_LOCATION | ZZZ-Z-9999 |

  Scenario Outline: Another caller may not reserve stock
    When I run "reserve_stock" with:
      | caller.role | now                      | idempotency_key | order_id | reserve_lines                                                                                                                 | stored_levels                                                                                                                                                                                     |
      | <role>      | 2026-11-22T10:00:00.000Z | reserve-0001    | ORD-1    | [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "quantity": 10}, {"sku": "GADGET-2", "location": "AMS-B-0143", "quantity": 5}] | [{"sku": "WIDGET-1", "location": "AMS-B-0142", "on_hand": 500, "reserved": 100, "available": 400}, {"sku": "GADGET-2", "location": "AMS-B-0143", "on_hand": 50, "reserved": 40, "available": 10}] |
    Then the output is "forbidden":
      | error_code | role   |
      | FORBIDDEN  | <role> |

    Examples:
      | role                 |
      | purchasing_system    |
      | warehouse_staff      |
      | warehouse_supervisor |
      | clock                |

